{% doc %}
  @description Return a hash that is safe to pass to the hash_merge filter. platformOS's `empty`
    literal (and nil) are NOT hashes, so the idiom `object.errors | default: empty` followed by
    `hash_merge` raises "first argument must be a hash". This normalizes any nil / empty / EmptyDrop
    errors value to a real, mergeable empty hash, while preserving an already-populated hash.
  @param {object} [errors] - existing errors container; may be nil, empty, or a populated hash.
  @returns {object} a real hash, safe for the hash_merge filter.
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign result = errors
  if result == blank
    assign result = {}
  endif
  return result
%}
